From: opencreator-os
Subject: [PATCH] uapi: binder: do not test a kernel config symbol

The vendor tree carries an old Android binder header that tests
CONFIG_ANDROID_BINDER_IPC_64BIT in a uapi file, which makes
`make headers_install` (OpenWrt's toolchain/kernel-headers) fail with
"leak CONFIG_ANDROID_BINDER_IPC_64BIT to user-space". Mainline dropped the
32-bit binder protocol; drop the test so the header always describes the
64-bit layout, as in mainline.

--- a/include/uapi/linux/android/binder.h
+++ b/include/uapi/linux/android/binder.h
@@ -24,10 +24,6 @@
 #include <linux/types.h>
 #include <linux/ioctl.h>
 
-#ifndef CONFIG_ANDROID_BINDER_IPC_64BIT
-#define BINDER_IPC_32BIT 1
-#endif
-
 #define B_PACK_CHARS(c1, c2, c3, c4) \
 	((((c1)<<24)) | (((c2)<<16)) | (((c3)<<8)) | (c4))
 #define B_TYPE_LARGE 0x85
